* Zero-knowledge\nin the Zama Protocol
** Single ZK role
*** ZKPoK on encrypted inputs
*** One packed proof per transaction, up to 2048 bits
*** Generated client-side in a browser or mobile app
*** Metered as a Gateway operation
** Proof system
*** TFHE-rs compact PKE proof
*** Derived from Libert, eprint 2023/800
*** ZKV1 close to the paper, ZKV2 by default
*** CRS produced by the KMS
*** ZkComputeLoad::Verify keeps proving cheap
** What the proof asserts
*** Knowledge of the plaintext
*** Ciphertext well-formed under the global FHE public key
*** Bound by metadata: contract, user, ACL, chain id
*** No statement about balances or business rules
** Verification path
*** Client SDK builds ciphertext + proof
*** Relayer forwards to the Gateway
*** Coprocessors verify the ZKPoK
*** Gateway runs majority consensus
*** Host chain checks EIP-712 coprocessor signatures\nin InputVerifier, not the proof itself
** Cryptography next door
*** FHE for computation on ciphertexts
*** Threshold MPC for key generation and decryption
*** KMS produces the CRS used by the proofs
*** Signatures, not ZK, carry decryption results back
** Limits and roadmap
*** ZKPoK is the non post-quantum component
*** Lattice-based replacement announced
*** ZK-MPC to verify KMS contributions
*** ZK-FHE to open coprocessing to anyone
@endmindmap
